      en: "The Batéké Plateaus in the Republic of Congo are a vast plateau in the southeastern part of the country. They cover 60,000 square kilometers, consisting of sandstone formations covered by savannah and forest. The average elevation is about 800 meters. The region is sparsely populated, primarily by the Teke people. The plateaus are important for livestock grazing and rain-fed agriculture. They host unique flora, including endemic orchids. The Batéké Plateaus are part of the transboundary Batéké-Léfini protected area.",
